  <h1>About KHOTWA</h1><p class="lead" style="margin-top:1rem;max-width:58ch">A student project built on one idea: every step makes a difference.</p></div></section>
 <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="prose"><h2>Why KHOTWA</h2><p>Khotwa means “step” in Arabic. Many young people do not know where to ask for help, or feel they cannot talk about what they are going through. KHOTWA brings information, prevention and human support together in one welcoming place.</p>
<h2>What we believe</h2><ul class="list-trail"><li>Support should come without judgment.</li><li>Progress is made of small steps, and each one counts.</li><li>Nobody should feel alone with their difficulties.</li></ul>
<h2>Who we are</h2><p>KHOTWA is a university web project created by a team of six students in Tunisia.</p>
<p class="alert">KHOTWA is not a medical service and does not replace professional care. If you or someone close to you is in danger, contact your local emergency number.</p></div></div></section>
